# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Generated protobuf Go files (api/gen/) are TRACKED SOURCE — NOT ignored.
# Go consumers fetch this module by tag and never run protoc, so the generated
# .pb.go / _grpc.pb.go ARE the published artifact and must be present at every
# commit and tag. They were previously gitignored + force-added, which let a
# plain `git add` silently drop new files and ship an incomplete module
# (ADR-0039 / sdk#63). They are now committed normally; the CI drift gate
# (`make generate && git diff --exit-code api/gen/`) keeps them in sync with the
# protos. Codegen is deterministic — plugin versions are pinned in the Makefile.

# NOTE: Taxonomy-generated files remain committed because taxonomy-gen lives in
# core/sdk/cmd/taxonomy-gen and depends on the full SDK module. These files are
# regenerated by 'make generate' but kept in version control so that consumers
# can build without running the generator. If taxonomy-gen is ever extracted to
# a standalone tool, these should also be gitignored:
#   graphrag/domain/domain_generated.go
#   graphrag/validation/validators_generated.go
#   graphrag/constants_generated.go
#   graphrag/query/query_generated.go
#   graphrag/helpers_generated.go
#   graphrag/taxonomy/relationships_generated.go
#   api/proto/taxonomy/v1/taxonomy.proto

# build artifacts (codegen binaries — protoc plugin, mission-docs-gen, mission-jsonschema-gen, etc.)
bin/
/mission-docs-gen
/mission-jsonschema-gen

# Rendered authz registry artifacts — these now live in core/gibson/internal/authz/registry/.
# The SDK still owns cmd/authz-registry-gen (the codegen tool) and the proto annotations.
# Defense-in-depth: block accidental re-commit of generated output here.
# Spec: private-authz-registry Task 5.
auth/registry/registry.yaml
auth/registry/registry.go
auth/registry/permissions.ts
gen/mission-authoring-bundle.tar.gz

# Compiled binaries must never be tracked (sdk#422). `make examples` and the
# codegen targets output to bin/ (ignored above); these paths guard against
# stray in-place `go build` runs re-committing them.
/authz-registry-gen
/cmd/taxonomy-gen/taxonomy-gen
/examples/custom-tool/custom-tool
/examples/minimal-agent/minimal-agent
